.\" Manpage for encfs
.TH encfs 1 "January 30, 2026" "1.0" "EncFS Variant Manual"

.SH NAME
encfs \- Encrypted Pass-Through File System (FUSE)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B encfs
mirror_dir mount_point
.RB [ \-o
.IR options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B encfs
is a cryptographic filesystem in userspace (FUSE). It transparently encrypts files stored in
.I mirror_dir
and makes them visible in plaintext at
.I mount_point
when mounted with the correct passphrase.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o passphrase=PASS
The passphrase used to derive the master encryption key via PBKDF2.

.TP
.B \-o mode=speed|secure
Sets the default encryption mode for new files.
.RS
.B speed
: Uses AES-256-CTR. Optimized for performance using Hybrid Block Compilation (Superblocks).
.br
.B secure
: Uses AES-256-GCM (Galois/Counter Mode). Provides authenticated encryption with per-block tags. (Default)
.RE

.TP
.B \-o allow_other
Allow other users to access the mount point (standard FUSE option).

.SH EXTENDED ATTRIBUTES
Special file operations are exposed via extended attributes (xattr).

.TP
.B user.enc_policy
Set the encryption policy for a file. Values:
.RS
.B Speed
: Switch to AES-CTR mode.
.br
.B Secure
: Switch to AES-GCM mode.
.br
.B ALL
: Encrypt all blocks (Default).
.br
.B HEAD:N
: Encrypt only the first N blocks (useful for huge media files).
.RE

.TP
.B user.zk_proof
Read-only attribute. Reading this attribute generates a (simulated) Zero-Knowledge Proof asserting that the filesystem possesses the decryption key for the file, without revealing the key or content.

.SH INTERNALS
.SS Metadata
One `.meta` file is created for every encrypted file. It stores the file-specific IV, encryption mode, policy, and a list of per-block IVs, Tags, and Hashes. The metadata file itself is integrity-protected by an HMAC-SHA256 signature appended to the end.

.SS Superblocks (Hybrid Block Compilation)
When `mode=speed` is active, the filesystem detects sequential I/O patterns. Requests larger than or equal to 32KB are processed as "Superblocks", reducing syscall overhead by batching encryption/decryption of 8 contiguous blocks.

.SH EXAMPLES

.B Mount with a secure mode:
.br
    $ ./encfs ./encrypted ./mnt -o passphrase=secret,mode=secure

.B Switch a specific file to speed mode:
.br
    $ setfattr -n user.enc_policy -v "Speed" ./mnt/video.mp4

.B Verify Key Possession (ZK Audit):
.br
    $ getfattr -n user.zk_proof ./mnt/sensitive.doc

.SH BUGS
Depending on the FUSE version, `allow_other` requires `user_allow_other` in `/etc/fuse.conf`.

.SH AUTHOR
